<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa seeks travel tie-up with NUR.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa seeks travel tie-up with NUR.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>German airline Lufthansa AG said on Thursday it wanted to intensify its relationship with travel group NUR and also sell its 18 pecent stake in travel and transport group Hapag Lloyd AG.</p>
<p>Lufthansa Chairman Juergen Weber told the airline's annual general meeting that Lufthansa's charter unit Condor was in talks with NUR, a unit of retail group Karstadt AG.</p>
<p>&quot;The leadership of Condor and NUR are holding talks over a closer working relationship,&quot; Weber said.</p>
<p>He gave no further details on how Condor and NUR would intensify their relationship.</p>
<p>Weber said Lufthansa would receive a &quot;good&quot; price for its 18 percent stake of Hapag when it was sold. But he declined to say when or to whom the Hapag stake would be sold.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
